A||N||12||Monkeyman||My custom center console||||10||
Z||000000||Monkeyman||11-08-2001||05:53 PM||||It's not quite finished yet, but it's finally in the car.  It still needs the new gauges wired up, the edges finished off (resanded and another coat or two of polyurethane) and some trim around the joints and around the HVAC controls.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/center_console-arm_rest.JPG"> <BR>I cut a piece out of the wood, added a piece of 1/2" foam and covered it with the same vinyl that resides on my doors (and my headliner--soon).<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/center_console-front.JPG"> <BR>I plan on adding my headlight and dimmer switch in between the window switches in the future.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/center_console-HVAC_controls.JPG"> <BR>ECM cover--It really needs some trim around it.  That'll go on this weekend.<P>The firewall and ledge under the rear window will be covered with the same wood (1/2" red oak plywood).<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/PontiacAPE.jpg">    <BR>Monkeyman||||reg||10
Z||000001||Jake_Dragon||11-08-2001||06:19 PM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/right.gif"> <BR>I was looking at some cherry with the same idea. <BR>You can get some edge veneer and use it to treat your plywood edges. <P><BR>------------------<BR>          <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/left.gif">                        <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_brow.gif">                       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/right.gif">           <BR>               <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/gt2_3.GIF">  <p>[This message has been edited by Jake_Dragon (edited 11-08-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Monkeyman||11-08-2001||06:28 PM||||Cherry, huh?  That was my original idea until I realized that my credit wasn't good enough for the loan I'd have to get.  (I wood ( <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">) have spent over $300 just for enough wood for the center console.  Then another $600 minimum to do the firewall.)  Damn expensive stuff.  So far I've only used up one 4x8 sheet of the plywood and that was almost $60.  I couldn't use boards as they don't make them wide enough to make the sides in one piece.  I wood ( <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">) have had to glue two boards together.  I think that wood ( <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">) have made it weaker.  If I had some straighter edges on the side pieces, I wood have used some trim, but I wanted the curves.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Cheever3000||11-08-2001||06:34 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>I wood have used some trim<HR></BLOCKQUOTE>You missed a smiley.<P>Looks real good.  Think it'll start warping after about 6 months or so?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> Just a little joke there.  Seriously, I like it!<P><BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Cheever_gold_sig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Philphine||11-08-2001||06:38 PM||||bit of glare so i can't tell, are the top circles guages or new center vents? and the heater controls are behind you? dose the cable part still work? all operational? if those four are all guages, what are they and are you using any of the stock ones? <P>looks interesting. i'd like to see the whole finished interior reworking. i remember you once saying you couldn't put in a fuel pump. i think you're underestimating yourself.<P>------------------<BR>Phil T.<P>start where you are,<BR>use what you have,<BR>do what you can.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Monkeyman||11-08-2001||08:11 PM||||Cheever3000--I just got tired of adding all of those smileys.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Philphine--Those are new center vents.  I still need to work up some sort of connection between them and the actual vent on the dash.  Most of the air ends up blowing out behind the console.  Maybe that will be a spring job.  The heat doesn't come out of the center vents anyway.  Yes.  The HVAC controls are behind me in the new ECM cover.  I tried to put them where the overhead lights are, but it just wasn't working.  I don't have the cable hooked up.  I'll definitely need a longer one.  Everything but the cable works fine.  Even the lights.  It's a little bit awkward to use the HVAC controls, but I don't change the settings very often.  I just use my left arm and reach around me.  If I had located the stereo a little higher, the HVAC controls would have fit but then I would have had to find another location for the switches.  If I had to do it again, I think I would have mounted the new gauges in A pillar pods (didn't think about that until after the fact).  I hope to have the entire interior finished (including new wood to replace the speaker grilles on the dash) in the next month or so.  I'll be sure to post pics then.  Installing a new fuel pump is alot different than this.  My wife helped out immensely (I think I spelled that wrong--sleepiness is taking its toll).  It's not as nice in person.  But it will be once all of the trim, etc is finished.||||reg||1
Z||000006||XDrewX||11-08-2001||09:00 PM||||You mentioned a vinyl headliner........<P>I dont have a sunroof, and my headliner needs to be replaced.<P>I was considering vinyl, but was afraid it would be too heavy, and the headliner would just end up sagging under the wieght or even collapsing.<P>Would you please share your method you plan on using.<P>If I remember right the headliner is only held in by the a-pillars and the overhead console.<P>By the way, that is a beautiful dash and console. Very custom !!!!!!!!<P>Thanks<P>Andrew||||reg||1
Z||000007||Monkeyman||11-09-2001||01:03 AM||||It's held in place by the A pillar trim, overhead light console, 3<sup>rd</sup> brake light assy (which I may decide to lose), sun visors (which I lost a while ago), clothes hooks, and (at least in my case) the sunroof opening.  If you don't have a sunroof, I would make sure that you strengthened the headliner board with fiberglas resin.  Maybe add some fiberglas mat around the 3<sup>rd</sup> brakelight and coat hanger areas just to be safe.  I just got one of the Fiero Stores fiberglas headliner boards, so I'm not worried about mine.||||reg||1
Z||000008||beer_stud_21||11-09-2001||02:59 AM||||Monkeyman,<P>Looks good.  You have done something simular to what I'm planning for my center console.  I wanted to ask you if you could post a close up of the center AC vents and if you could tell me where you got them from?  I have been looking for a source for AC vents.<P>-Marlin||||reg||1
Z||000009||artherd||11-09-2001||03:09 AM||||Wow! Really nice looking.  I don't normally dig the whole wood-in-a-car thing, but I really do like what you've done!<P>Totally unique, the air vents really set it off and the whole thing has a very handcrafted, balanced, and thought-out appeal!<P>Big thumbs up on the whole project man!<P>Best!<BR>Ben<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000010||Monkeyman||11-09-2001||05:08 AM||||artherd--Thanx.  I was always more of a modern type of guy until my wife talked me into this.  Now I'm glad I did it.  <P>beer_stud--I'll snap some pics this afternoon.  I found those at a local car show.  The vendors name was 'A Plus Hot Rod Shop' out of Chandler, IN (around Evansville).  I think I paid $17 for the pair.  I wanted a set of black anodized aluminum ones that are more flaps than this, but they were around $100.||||reg||1
